                <pb facs="1555" n="1397" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1397"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Leishman
                        to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 68.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my dispatch, No. 63, of
                    the 18th instant, in which I had the honor to inform you of the difficulties
                    experienced <pb facs="1556" n="1398" xml:id="pg1398"/> by Mr. Fowle and Mr.
                    MacDowell, two of our missionaries, while traveling in the interior of Turkey, I
                    beg to inform the department that I am in receipt of the following telegram from
                    Mr. Fowle, informing me that the awaited permission has been granted him: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>With the permission of the local authority I am going to Istanos and we
                            are thankful to you.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fowle.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>It is peculiarly gratifying to the embassy that the exercise of a patient
                    pressure sufficed to bring about this result.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John G. A.
                    Leishman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
